WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.560
Hey! Where are you, Tokine?

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.830
Stop hiding and show yourself!

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.830
Can you not call out to me
like I'm some Ayakashi?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Um. I made a new cake.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.040
You brought one over again?

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.910
You're obsessed with cakes. Yoshi.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.550
You really shouldn't come to
Karasumori like it's some kind of picnic trip.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.350
I think this one came out really well.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.150
Try it out for me.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.620
Oh fine.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.640
Umm...

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.570
What is this?!

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.780
If you have time to
make stuff like this...

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.770
you should be training more
on the Kekkai techniques!

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.710
You're so cool, honey.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.540
She shot you down.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.290
Sumimura Yoshimori and
Yukimura Tokine protect

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.790
the Karasumori Site from the Ayakashi.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.250
It is an ancestral mission that has been
passed down to them.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.830
Just because it's New Year's
doesn't mean you can rest!

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.090
Right! Let's work hard this year too!

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.940
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.810
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.010
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.910
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.350
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.750
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.290
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.630
I will protect you that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:46.300
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.800
Sha la la la la...

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:57.210
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.180
(Secret romance)

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:04.390
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.150
(A strange distance)

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:12.990
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.060
Yeah

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:17.530
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.140
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:26.470
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.130
What's wrong, Yoshimori?

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.700
You haven't even finished
making your cake.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.170
I brought some cake to Tokine,
but she didn't like it.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.940
Don't tell me that your passion
is extinguished because of that?!

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:03.970
Kind of.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.680
Well, umm. I actually think it's good
that you're doing stuff like this!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:09.550
Uh-huh.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:11.990
What should I do?

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.920
At this rate Yoshimori will
give up on his dream!

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.880
I must do something!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.050
I know!

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.260
Yoshimori, I'll get you to eat
the best kind of cake!

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.730
Huh? The best kind of cake?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.940
Yeah. There was a time when my passion
for literature was waning

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.700
so your mother bought
some cake for me.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.640
That cake tasted so dreamy.
It filled me with energy!

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.710
Sweets have the amazing power
to do that.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.340
R-Really?

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.220
All right! Let's meet at
the bronze natto statue

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.320
in front of the station
at 3:30 tomorrow.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:51.550
Okay...

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.800
He's not coming at all.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.740
Oh... uh...

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.250
Hey, Toshimori...
What are you doing?

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:21.890
What am I doing?

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:24.380
This isn't the place
we're supposed to meet.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.600
Huh?! Really?

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.790
Yeah. We said yesterday that
we'd meet at the bronze natto statue.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.360
This is the bronze pigeon [hato] statue.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.070
Oh right.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.840
But I was supposed to meet up
with Dad.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.830
Dad can't come out because
he has a deadline.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.710
So you came in his place?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.340
Yeah.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.420
Dad gave me his wallet and
told me to go buy it with you.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.380
CASTLE CHÂTEAU BERG

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.360
Isn't this the back exit?

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.200
Yup, because it's top secret.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.300
It says "Once a week,
they pass out tickets for you to buy...

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.300
the legendary Castle Château Berg's
special chocolate cake."

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.640
Legendary chocolate cake?!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:18.010
Yup, its taste is legendary!
Or so this says.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.440
Let me see that note.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.880
The use of chocolate is as delicate
as their store's name suggests.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.850
The cake has seven layers,
giving it a complex flavor.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:33.690
- The fragrance and flavor of chocolate
- give it more of a special accent.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.560
Words can't express
how good it tastes.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.000
By the time I came to my senses
tears were streaming down my face.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.060
Drool too.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.400
"Drool too," he says.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.810
Whoa! Awesome!

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.080
There are seven seats this week.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.050
So they're not going to
sell more than seven.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:57.290
"After eating this, you will remember
your burning passion, Yoshimori.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.780
"Good luck."
That's what he says.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.680
Wait, this doesn't say when
they're passing out the tickets.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.620
What? Isn't that the most important part?

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.660
Are they going to pass out
the tickets now?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.490
We're the first ones.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:19.240
Ticket distribution scheduled for
tomorrow at 5 a.m. Limited to seven.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.210
They're passing it out at five
in the morning tomorrow?!

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:21.870
Looks like it.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.470
I have my Kekkaishi duties at that time.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.110
Why not have Tokine handle that then?

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.640
I can't do that!

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.750
Then are you going to give up
on the cake?

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.340
No, I have a plan.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.750
Shiki!

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.290
You're going to get a Shikigami
to line up for you?

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.690
I don't think that's a very legitimate
way of using them.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.690
So you don't want any of
the cake. Toshimori?

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.230
That's beside the point.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:46.820
Huh?

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:51.210
Who are you?!

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.780
Do I look that chubby to you? Huh?!

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.010
You don't have to make it look like you.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.410
Do it over!
And put some heart into it!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.210
You really don't need to get
so serious about it.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:06.520
No! How well I use a Shikigami
shows the skills of a Caster!

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.280
But!

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:10.850
Letting this happen will be
beneath my kokan [groin]!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.120
You mean it's beneath
your koken [dignity].

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.230
Be more elegant and manly!

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.470
You rang?

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.270
A crazier one appeared!

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.850
What's with those sideburns?

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.370
Oh. Screw this!

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.210
Huh?!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.140
Line up for me, okay?!
I'm busy right now!

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.280
Roger!

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.920
"Roger"? I won't be responsible
for what's going to happen.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.550
I'm going home!

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.290
Is that him?!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.960
Joso. Ketsu!

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.230
Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:55.730
Ketsu!

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:02.800
Ow! Hot!

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.340
You're terrible at this.
Can't you aim better?!

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.410
Shut up! Just leave it to me!

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:18.860
Something's weird, honey.
Yoshi is already tired today.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:22.130
Yoshimori, if you're not feeling well,
maybe you should rest.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.660
I'm said... I'm fine!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.430
Shoot! Did I use up too much strength
on the Shikigami?!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.970
Straighten up!

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.780
It sure has been a while
since I came here.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.810
I wonder if Yoshimori's Shikigami
is lined up here.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.880
Wow looks like this store is
as popular as ever.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.890
I wonder if that's Yoshimori's Shikigami?

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:52.760
Whoa?!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:53.890
Outta my way!

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.230
Huh?!

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.800
This is the place, boss!
With the legendary cake!

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.730
Oh? You.
Plenty of people lined up already.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.500
Hey, bro. You mind if you let me cut?

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.170
What are you doing?!
Everyone's already lined up!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:21.210
Sorry, man.
My girl says that she wants it.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.060
Cut me some slack.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:27.120
What was that?
You'll give me your place in line? Thanks!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.900
Oh? Is everyone going to
give up their spots too?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.730
I can't let this go unpunished!

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:43.140
I'll make them eat the ground
'til they bleed with my fists of justice!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:52.240
That's what I want to say,
but I'm just not good at fighting...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.680
What should I do?

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.320
Wait just a second!

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.090
What?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.850
Stop this!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.650
You appeared out of nowhere and
are being too unreasonable!

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.120
There goes Yoshimori's Shikigami.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.000
Stop this!

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.640
You appeared out of nowhere
and are being too unreasonable!

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:16.970
H-He's so weak...

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.880
That's not enough!

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.280
W-What's with him?

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:24.550
You're creeping me out!

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.140
I'll melt you like a piece of chocolate!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.950
Oh no! Shikigami-kun!

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.060
Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.220
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.490
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.300
Metsu!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:43.660
Ketsu!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.140
Why you!

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:52.740
Why you!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.490
What are you doing?!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:00.990
Huh?

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.820
For these, you just designate
a position and...

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.620
You look worn out...

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.460
Shut up.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.790
My Shikigami is about to disappear.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.190
Did some accident happen?

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.470
Come on!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.140
Yeah!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.480
But I already set up some insurance.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.010
This isn't enough yet!

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.140
Shut up!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.350
Stop it!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.800
Beat them all down!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.360
W-What's going on?!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:48.770
Secret Arts!

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:49.430
Joso!

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:51.770
The Tornado...

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.670
Ketsu!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.510
Of Passion!

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.040
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.150
Metsu!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:09.420
Hey!

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.260
You're wasting your strength
against such a tiny target again!

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:15.020
I beat it... didn't... I?

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.890
Hey, what's wrong with you?

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.770
It seems that I have kicked
unnecessary things again.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.940
That's your catch phrase?!

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:30.910
So he used his final weapon.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:31.870
Huh?

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:36.310
You were using your Shikigami
elsewhere, weren't you?

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.220
So that's why Yoshi was
looking so tired.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.960
Thanks to that, I managed to secure
a ticket for the chocolate cake.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.460
What?! How dare you
even call yourself a Caster!

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:49.460
Huh?

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.730
What if a really strong enemy came?!

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.130
You would have been dead!

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:57.070
You don't need to be so mad, honey.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.800
We only got a weakling enemy
today anyway.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.400
I'm just disappointed in myself
for worrying about you!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.610
I don't even want to talk
to you anymore!

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.780
Hey you...
Why are you frozen like that?

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.490
That Yoshimori...

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.190
Will he ever grow out of
being such a cake otaku?

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.380
Excuse me...

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.960
What do you want?

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:01.400
I... Uh...

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.940
Is Uncle Shuji there?

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.600
Dad? He went out to deliver
his manuscript.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.240
Oh. Then what about Toshimori-kun?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.650
He's at a friend's house.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:18.720
Then never mind!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.410
Hey wait!

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.320
I don't really understand,
but can't Grandpa Shige help you?

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.760
I don't want to ask him for help on this.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.530
Then what about me?

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:31.090
Hmm...

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.730
She actually has to think about it?!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.330
You see... Something black
appeared inside my house.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.770
What?! Is there some ghost
haunting your house?!

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:41.630
That's terrible!

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:46.900
I know! It's black and round and
shiny and scuffles around!

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.550
That thing!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.180
Is that a...

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.850
Don't say its name!

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.890
What if you said its name and
it appeared?!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.220
I wouldn't be able to stand it!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.100
Tokine!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.200
Don't leave me alone in the house!

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.160
Tokine!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.400
Oh!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.700
Why did you bring that brat over?!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.440
There was no one else.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:17.340
How pitiful to have to resort to
asking this brat for help!

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:21.100
I'm sorry. Usually, Mom is the one
that usually takes care of it,

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.520
but she's taking a trip to
the hot springs right now.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.050
Now that I think about it

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:28.050
this is the first time I've actually come
inside Tokine's house.

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.080
Excuse me!

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.530
Is Tokine's room over here?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.390
The kitchen is this way.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:46.970
It's not here.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:48.200
No! It's somewhere!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:55.710
I can feel its presence!
I know it's hiding somewhere!

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:59.940
You got some radar there.
Are you Hakubi or Madarao now?

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.020
Just go find it and take care of it!

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:10.830
I can smell her shampoo.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:16.060
Yoshimori! Hurry up and find it!
Concentrate!

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.670
I can't concentrate like this!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.680
Hurry! Hurry!

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.840
Oh. I uh...

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.710
Ketsu!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:32.910
Huh?

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:37.020
Why are you building
a Kekkai over your head?!

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.230
Mom would have taken care
of that with her slippers

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.260
in under three seconds!

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.130
And why are you using Kekkai?!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.130
The pieces will fly all around this room!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:50.060
Wait, isn't Auntie always crushing it
with the slippers?

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.840
Mom's a pro.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:58.070
She uses the exact amount of strength
so that the innards won't splash out.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.980
That's scary!

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:06.850
Just hurry up and take care of it!
In five minutes!

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.690
No, under ten seconds! You got that?!

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.520
Now you're just being self-centered!

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.390
Sorry.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:17.020
But...

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:22.730
I just... I just can't stand those things.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.580
All right. I'll think about what to do.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.330
What are you doing with
the newspapers?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.660
I'm going to lay them out
all around here.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.660
I just noticed this recently,

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.760
but if you designate the position
of the Kekkai

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.140
on the ground or in the air,
you can't move them...

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.480
but if you place them over things
like pieces of paper...

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.470
See? You can move it.

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:10.550
Oh, so you're going to control conditions
rather than control coordinates.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:14.110
Huh? I don't know the specifics of it.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:19.090
But after thinking about it,
the Kekkai techniques are really random.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:21.100
Depending on the timing of
the formation.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.720
You can engulf things and
even pick stuff up.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.170
That's why they're really versatile.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.070
Well, I guess so...

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:30.640
Don't you read the lesson scrolls?

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.470
Huh? You know how to read
those weird scrolls?

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:37.650
It's easy. Once you read them,
you'll learn a lot!

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:39.440
O-Oh?

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.150
So he figured this out on his own...

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.680
He really has good intuition
when it comes to the techniques.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:50.830
Anyway, I'll catch it this way
and take it outside.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.160
Then I'll take care of it
where you can't see.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.220
Is that good enough for you?

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.260
Yeah...

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.130
All right. Now everything's ready.

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.100
Come out, my ultimate Shikigami!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.770
You rang?!

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.650
What's with this design?
And they're so small.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.350
That's what makes them perfect
for the job.

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:21.680
Run around the kitchen and
try to chase the target onto the newspaper!

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:23.280
Roger!

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.050
Now bring it on!

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:33.490
Yoshimori!

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:39.170
A-Am I being depended on right now?!

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.010
There it is!

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:44.150
Tornado yet again!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.580
Just you wait, Tokine!

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:47.170
I'll take care of it right away!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.050
No!

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.560
Hey!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.960
No!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.100
No!

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.100
I'm sorry, Yoshimori!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:18.110
Shikigami-kun got us
seven of the chocolate cakes.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:20.700
But we were out of snacks and...

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:25.090
Heh. Such a fancy little thing!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.520
This is disgusting!

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:31.250
This is so good!

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:34.220
I just love this taste!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:40.760
Oh? There's one left.
You mustn't waste food, you know!

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:46.800
This is truly disgusting.
So disgusting!

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.400
I'm so sorry, Yoshimori!

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:57.250
It's all right, Dad. I don't mind.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:01.250
And ever since that incident
with the black thing

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.650
Tokine stopped talking to me.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.220
Well. More like...

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.730
Tokine! 'Morning.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:16.470
Hey.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.230
Maybe she really hates me now.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:29.350
Hey! Are you okay?!

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:30.410
Yoshimori!

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:35.180
I'm sorry about what happened
the other day.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:45.490
Huh? Hey! What's this?

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:50.470
"This is thanks for the other day."

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:54.800
So she's telling me to never wear
that shirt again?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.540
So it's not that she hates you.

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:00.770
So that's what it is.
Could this be?!

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:02.950
It's the chocolate cake from that store!

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:10.950
Whoa! It's so good
it's out of this world!

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:18.230
I get it! Tokine wants me to make
a cake as good as this!

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:19.430
You think so?

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.900
It just seems like an ordinary token
of appreciation to me.

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.070
Just you wait Tokine!

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:27.170
I'll make something like this one day!

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.730
Why is he so energetic?

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:32.340
It's youth, honey.

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:47.060
The breeze blows past us
in this city we know so well

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:53.760
The two of us both walk at our usual pace

00:22:55.340 --> 00:23:03.140
Joking around I noticed after I laughed

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:09.480
Your mature look that
I had never seen before

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:19.330
You don't have to say anything it's okay

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:25.690
I'm not mistaking these feelings

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:34.780
Straight ahead I'm pushing forward

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:42.310
Yet I can't help but keep gazing at you

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:51.290
Even if we are near or far

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:59.860
The red string connects one to another
